## VS Code Timeline: Context Menu Items


### Local History Entries

These are the auto-saved snapshots that VS Code creates as you work.

| Menu Item | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Compare with File** | Opens a side-by-side diff editor comparing the selected snapshot against the **current version of the file on disk**. This is the same as left-clicking the entry. |
| **Compare with Previous** | Opens a diff editor comparing this snapshot against the **immediately preceding local history entry** for the same file. This shows the delta of changes between two consecutive saves. |
| **Select for Compare** | Marks this snapshot as the **base** (left side) of a two-step comparison. After selecting this, right-click another entry and choose **Compare with Selected** to diff any two arbitrary snapshots — they do not need to be consecutive. |
| **Show Contents** | Opens the snapshot in a read-only editor tab. This lets you inspect the file contents at that point in time without modifying the current file on disk. Unlike left-clicking, this does not open a diff. |
| **Restore Contents** | Overwrites the current file on disk with the contents of this snapshot. This is a destructive action — it replaces the live file, so use it when you want to roll back to a previous state. |
| **Reveal in File Explorer** | Opens your operating system's file manager (Windows Explorer, macOS Finder, etc.) and highlights the file's location in the workspace. |
| **Rename** | Assigns a custom label to the snapshot (e.g., "Before API refactor"). By default, snapshots are named by timestamp and trigger type (File Saved, Workspace Edit). Renaming makes it easier to identify important milestones. |
| **Delete** | Permanently removes the snapshot from VS Code's local history storage. This frees up disk space and declutters the Timeline. Deleted snapshots cannot be recovered. |

{{::il.Vscode_TimelineLocalEntryRightClick_img}}


### Git Entries

These represent commits from the Git repository that touched the current file.

| Menu Item | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Open Changes** | Opens a diff editor showing the changes introduced by **this commit only** — that is, the diff between this commit and its immediate parent. This is the same as left-clicking the entry. |
| **Open Commit** | Opens the full commit details in a multi-file diff editor. Unlike **Open Changes** (which only shows the current file), this shows every file that was modified in that commit, letting you see the complete change set. |
| **Open on GitHub** | Opens the commit's page in your default web browser on GitHub. This requires that the repository has a GitHub remote configured and that you have internet access. |
| **Select for Compare** | Marks this commit as the **base** (left side) of a two-step comparison. After selecting this, right-click another commit and choose **Compare with Selected** to see the cumulative diff between any two commits in the file's history. |
| **Copy Commit Hash** | Copies the full 40-character SHA-1 hash of the commit to your clipboard. |
| **Copy Commit Message** | Copies the commit's message text to your clipboard. |

{{::il.Vscode_TimelineGitEntryRightClick_img}}

